<header><p class="st-kicker">theocracy · Arabia and the Gulf</p><h1 class="st-title">Najdiyya</h1><p class="st-meta">685 CE – 693 CE (approx.) · capital al-Yamama</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A Kharijite state in central and eastern Arabia that briefly ruled al-Yamama, Bahrain and Oman during the civil war of the 680s.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Najdiyya took their name from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/najda-ibn-amir-al-hanafi">Najda ibn Amir al-Hanafi</a>, a Kharijite leader who broke with the more extreme <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/azariqa">Azariqa</a>. During the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-fitna">Second Fitna</a> he seized al-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yamama">Yamama</a>, his tribe's homeland in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/najd">Najd</a>, around 686 and was acknowledged as commander of the faithful by his followers.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/najda-ibn-amir-al-hanafi">Najda</a>'s forces conquered <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/sheikhdom-of-bahrain">Bahrain</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oman">Oman</a> and parts of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/republic-of-yemen">Yemen</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-hadramawt">Hadramawt</a> and threatened <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taif">Ta'if</a>, challenging the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/caliphate-of-ibn-al-zubayr">Caliphate of Ibn al-Zubayr</a>. He was more moderate than other <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kharijites">Kharijites</a>, allowing those who did not join him to live unharmed and relying on reasoned judgement where the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/quran">Quran</a> was silent. Internal disputes over the treatment of captives and payments to followers divided the movement.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Around 691 his own followers deposed and killed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/najda-ibn-amir-al-hanafi">Najda</a> and turned to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abu-fudayk">Abu Fudayk</a>. After the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/umayyad-caliphate">Umayyads</a> reunited the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliphate</a>, an army sent by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abd-al-malik-ibn-marwan">Abd al-Malik</a> defeated Abu Fudayk in <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/sheikhdom-of-bahrain">Bahrain</a> in 693, ending the state.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="theocracy, 685 CE – 693 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M30 82 V46 Q50 12 70 46 V82 Z"/><path d="M50 30 V82 M40 58 H60"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">theocracy</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Arabia and the Gulf</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:73.33%;width:1.20%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>685 CE – 693 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>theocracy</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>theocratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>al-Yamama</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Najda ibn Amir al-Hanafi, Abu Fudayk</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Kharijite Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Arabic</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/saudi-arabia">Saudi Arabia</a>, <a href="/countries/bahrain">Bahrain</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Najdat, Najdite state</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=689&amp;focus=najdiyya" aria-label="Najdiyya on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5867 1304 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Najdiyya lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M6134 1224h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6187 1560h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M6187 1560h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day Saudi Arabia. <a href="/atlas?year=689&amp;focus=najdiyya">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

